       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. The usual maximum single dose is 850 mg to 1,000 mg. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum. It may be what you meant if \"1700\" was a typo.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another regimen.** Tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Pharmacy will probably flag it either way."
      }
